  {
    "kind": "markdown",
    "source": "## 2. Sample data and BYOD contract\n\nThe default sample is a deterministic, three-variate **hourly** panel with trend, daily seasonality, weekly modulation, correlation between variates, and seeded noise. It is intentionally simple enough to inspect while still giving naïve and foundation-model forecasts something non-trivial to do.\n\nThe sample contains:\n\n- **432 hourly observations** per variate;\n- three target columns;\n- a 48-step validation future;\n- a later 48-step independent test future; and\n- a 24-step seasonal-naïve period.\n\n### BYOD\n\nSet `USE_BYOD=True` and provide `BYOD_PATH` to a local CSV. The file must contain:\n\n- a unique `timestamp` column;\n- one or more additional finite numeric target columns;\n- unique, strictly increasing timestamps;\n- exactly hourly spacing; and\n- enough history for two non-overlapping future holdouts plus the seasonal baseline.\n\nThe BYOD path uses the same validation, chronological splitting, model execution, evaluation, and export semantics as the sample path. Data stays inside the notebook runtime; the models are downloaded from their public upstream hosts, but your target values are not sent to a DIMER service or inference API.\n\nDo not use confidential, restricted, regulated, sensitive, or personal data in a hosted runtime unless you are authorized to process it there.\n"
  },
