  {
    "kind": "markdown",
    "source": "## 6. Evaluate every model under one metric contract\n\nFor every model and baseline we compute:\n\n- **MAE** — average absolute error in the target's original units;\n- **RMSE** — like MAE, but penalizes large misses more strongly;\n- **sMAPE** — scale-normalized absolute percentage error (reported as a percentage);\n- **mean pinball loss** over q10/q50/q90 for probabilistic model outputs; and\n- **q10–q90 coverage** — the fraction of held-out values inside the model's outer forecast quantiles.\n\nCoverage is **descriptive**, not a calibration guarantee. The interval is a model quantile band. A single synthetic holdout cannot establish frequentist coverage on an unseen deployment domain.\n\nThe naïve baselines have only point forecasts, so pinball loss and interval coverage are recorded as not applicable.\n"
  },
  {
    "kind": "code",
    "source": "# @title 6.1 Compute validation and independent-test metrics\ndef point_metrics(actual, predicted):\n    actual = np.asarray(actual, dtype=float)\n    predicted = np.asarray(predicted, dtype=float)\n    error = predicted - actual\n    denom = np.abs(actual) + np.abs(predicted)\n    smape = np.mean(np.where(denom > 1e-12, 2 * np.abs(error) / denom, 0.0)) * 100\n    return {\n        \"mae\": float(np.mean(np.abs(error))),\n        \"rmse\": float(np.sqrt(np.mean(error ** 2))),\n        \"smape_pct\": float(smape),\n    }\n\ndef pinball(actual, forecast, q):\n    delta = np.asarray(actual) - np.asarray(forecast)\n    return float(np.mean(np.maximum(q * delta, (q - 1) * delta)))\n\ndef probabilistic_metrics(actual, quantiles, levels):\n    scores = [pinball(actual, quantiles[:, index, :], q) for index, q in enumerate(levels)]\n    q10 = quantiles[:, levels.index(0.1), :]\n    q90 = quantiles[:, levels.index(0.9), :]\n    coverage = np.mean((actual >= q10) & (actual <= q90))\n    return {\n        \"mean_pinball_q10_q50_q90\": float(np.mean(scores)),\n        \"q10_q90_coverage\": float(coverage),\n    }\n\nmetric_rows = []\nprediction_store = {}\n\nfor partition, actual in [(\"validation\", validation_truth), (\"test\", test_truth)]:\n    for baseline_name, baseline_parts in BASELINES.items():\n        pred = baseline_parts[partition]\n        row = {\"partition\": partition, \"condition\": baseline_name, \"kind\": \"baseline\", **point_metrics(actual, pred)}\n        row.update({\"mean_pinball_q10_q50_q90\": np.nan, \"q10_q90_coverage\": np.nan})\n        metric_rows.append(row)\n        prediction_store[(partition, baseline_name)] = {\"median\": pred, \"quantiles\": None, \"levels\": None}\n\n    for key, result in MODEL_RESULTS.items():\n        quantiles = np.asarray(result[f\"{partition}_quantiles\"], dtype=float)\n        levels = [float(x) for x in result[\"quantile_levels\"]]\n        median = quantiles[:, levels.index(0.5), :]\n        row = {\n            \"partition\": partition,\n            \"condition\": key,\n            \"kind\": \"foundation_model\",\n            **point_metrics(actual, median),\n            **probabilistic_metrics(actual, quantiles, levels),\n            \"wall_seconds\": float(result[\"wall_seconds\"]),\n            \"device\": result[\"runtime\"][\"device\"],\n        }\n        metric_rows.append(row)\n        prediction_store[(partition, key)] = {\"median\": median, \"quantiles\": quantiles, \"levels\": levels}\n\nmetrics = pd.DataFrame(metric_rows)\ndisplay(metrics.sort_values([\"partition\", \"mae\"]))\n"
  },
  {
    "kind": "markdown",
    "source": "## 7. Freeze a validation decision before reading the final test\n\nFor the workshop exercise, the selected foundation model is the one with the **lowest aggregate validation MAE**. This rule is declared before the test comparison is read.\n\nThat is intentionally modest: one validation window does not establish a globally superior model. It only creates a reproducible decision rule for this sample so that we can demonstrate the difference between **selection evidence** and **independent test evidence**.\n\nThe later test window is not used to change the selection.\n"
  },
